          "align": "justify",
          "cols": 1,
          "text": "Four columns in dynamic balance\n\nTurning Point was conceived, designed and built at Anant University. The structure was cut from cor-ten sheet and folded into boxes, each one perforated with a part of a single pattern that grows from the base to the top.\n\nThe pattern is a reaction–diffusion simulation, tuned so that it stays connected and never leaves a floating island of steel.\n\nTurning Point was conceived, designed and built at Anant University. The structure was cut from cor-ten sheet and folded into boxes, each one perforated with a part of a single pattern that grows from the base to the top.\n\nThe pattern is a reaction–diffusion simulation, tuned so that it stays connected and never leaves a floating island of steel.",
